      "content": "Monitoring yourself for side effects like bruising is not a substitute for regular INR blood testing when taking warfarin. Adjusting dosage without medical guidance risks bringing your INR out of the therapeutic range, which can be dangerous. You must work with your healthcare provider to find a safe Vitamin K dose or an alternative supplement that won't interfere with your blood thinner.",
      "source": "target",
